        "title": "refactor: split oversized test suites",
        "body": "Closes #106350\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a maintenance problem where five core test suites had grown to roughly 9,500–13,800 lines each, making navigation, ownership review, and focused changes unnecessarily difficult.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach existing `*.test.ts` remains the sole Vitest entry and imports cohesive `*.test-support.ts` modules plus a narrowly shared harness. This preserves the original mocked module graph and runtime ordering; independent test entries were rejected because non-isolated Vitest workers can retain singleton state between files.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible or runtime behavior change. Maintainers get focused modules capped at 2,273 lines instead of five 9,500–13,800-line files. No changelog entry because this is test-only.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact AST registration audit: 1,123 declarations preserved with zero missing or extra titles (`294 + 262 + 214 + 136 + 217`).\n- Exact-head Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxdnsmr6bxxzj3rt49x2gmy9`: all five entries passed, 1,299 expanded tests across three Vitest shards.\n- Same exact-head Testbox: `pnpm check:changed` passed all four typecheck lanes, core/extension lint, database-first, sidecar, import-cycle, webhook, and pairing guards in 13m09s.\n- Initial hosted CI showed `.test-support.ts` was not excluded by every production-only guard. The split modules now use the recognized `.test-utils.ts` suffix; the fresh full gate passes.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Automatic autoreview was attempted again after the CI fix and failed closed because the mechanical move is a 3.7 MB no-rename patch over its 180 KB bundle limit. Equivalent manual review used the exact registration multiset, entry-only reachability check, shared-harness dependency pruning, suffix classification, focused tests, and the full changed gate.\n",
